meta {
  name: Update Personal Details (Student)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/application-forms/my-applications/{{applicationId}}/personal-details
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "full_name": "Rahul Sharma",
    "date_of_birth": "2005-06-15",
    "gender": "male",
    "category": "General",
    "blood_group": "O+",
    "religion": "Hindu",
    "mother_tongue": "Hindi",
    "marital_status": "single",
    "aadhar_number": "123456789012",
    "profile_photo_url": null,
    "email": "rahul.sharma@example.com",
    "mobile_country_code": "+91",
    "mobile_number": "9876543210",
    "whatsapp_country_code": "+91",
    "whatsapp_number": "9876543210"
  }
}

docs {
  Full-replace write of the personal-details step (409 if the application
  has already been submitted). The URL still takes an application id (used
  only for the ownership/draft/paid gate), but the actual data now lands
  on the Student profile, not this Application row — reusable across every
  application the same student submits. `profile_photo_url` /
  `whatsapp_country_code` / `whatsapp_number` are the one exception: still
  stored as top-level Application columns, accepted together here since
  they're conceptually part of "personal info." `email` / `mobile_number`
  are new contact fields shown on the redesigned Personal Information
  screen — deliberately separate from the student's login `Student.email`
  (never overwritten by this endpoint). Advances currentStep to at least
  3. Application only gets its own frozen copy of personal_details once,
  at Submit Application (the point-in-time snapshot) — see
  Get Application Form Details to read the live (pre-submit) values.
}
